UPDATE services SET title='Custom Web Apps', summary='Internal tools, portals and operations dashboards built around how your company already works — not around a vendor''s idea of it.',
  body_md='Off-the-shelf software makes your team adapt to it. We build the opposite: web applications shaped around the way your company already works, running on your own infrastructure, using your own data.

**What that looks like in practice**

- One screen that replaces a six-system copy-and-paste job when a new product is added
- A purchasing tool that computes reorder points from real sales velocity instead of gut feel
- A statement importer that reads CSV, Excel and scanned PDFs and categorises the lines for you
- A client intake portal with no login, that turns a completed questionnaire into a tracked account
- Scan stations for receiving, packing and cycle counts that write straight into the ERP you already run

**How they are built**

Server-rendered or single-page, whichever suits the job. PostgreSQL or your existing SQL Server. Plain-SQL migrations that run at boot, so a deploy is one command. Docker Compose with healthchecks, so the same stack runs on your server as on ours. Role-based login, and — where it makes sense — authentication against the user table your ERP already maintains, so there is no second list of people to keep in step.

You get the repository, the installer and documentation your next hire can read.', body_html='<p>Off-the-shelf software makes your team adapt to it. We build the opposite: web applications shaped around the way your company already works, running on your own infrastructure, using your own data.</p>
<p><strong>What that looks like in practice</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>One screen that replaces a six-system copy-and-paste job when a new product is added</li>
<li>A purchasing tool that computes reorder points from real sales velocity instead of gut feel</li>
<li>A statement importer that reads CSV, Excel and scanned PDFs and categorises the lines for you</li>
<li>A client intake portal with no login, that turns a completed questionnaire into a tracked account</li>
<li>Scan stations for receiving, packing and cycle counts that write straight into the ERP you already run</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>How they are built</strong></p>
<p>Server-rendered or single-page, whichever suits the job. PostgreSQL or your existing SQL Server. Plain-SQL migrations that run at boot, so a deploy is one command. Docker Compose with healthchecks, so the same stack runs on your server as on ours. Role-based login, and — where it makes sense — authentication against the user table your ERP already maintains, so there is no second list of people to keep in step.</p>
<p>You get the repository, the installer and documentation your next hire can read.</p>', is_published=true, updated_at=now()
WHERE slug='custom-web-apps';
UPDATE services SET title='Mobile & Scanner Apps', summary='Warehouse and field tools that work on the phone or scanner in your team''s hand — capturing data where the work actually happens.',
  body_md='When the work happens away from a desk — at a receiving door, in an aisle, on a delivery route — a mobile tool is the difference between data entered now and data entered never.

**What we build**

- Barcode scan-and-verify for inbound deliveries, so a short shipment is caught at the door rather than at month end
- Bin and slot location tracking, with quantity adjustments made in the aisle
- Two-scan pack and check stations, with each scan attributed to the person who made it
- Mobile cycle counts that write to an audit table instead of a clipboard

**Design decisions that matter on a floor**

These are built as responsive web apps, which means no app store, no device enrolment, and no version drift across a fleet of handhelds. They run on the scanners and phones you already own, and an update is a page refresh.

Where they have logins, they authenticate against your existing ERP user tables, so a new hire is added once in the system where staff are already managed — and someone disabled there is locked out of the floor immediately. Every write carries a user and a timestamp. Accountability is the point, not a side effect.

See the [warehouse floor suite](/work/warehouse-floor-suite) for four of these running in one building.', body_html='<p>When the work happens away from a desk — at a receiving door, in an aisle, on a delivery route — a mobile tool is the difference between data entered now and data entered never.</p>
